\textbf{Verification}. The claim that one algorithm runs everywhere is only
worth making if it is tested. A single command runs every experiment over every
radio-free physical layer, walks 44 command-line flags and 82 topology settings
from the text a user types through to the object each one configures, and
launches multi-node topologies as real processes.
